<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Launcher-icon palette, kept in its own file rather than colors.xml.

  These are icon-specific tokens: they exist to make the mic glyph read at
  48dp against a launcher wallpaper, which is a different problem from the
  in-app surfaces colors.xml describes. Mixing them would invite someone to
  "unify" the two and flatten the icon's contrast.

  The glow pair is deliberately the SAME hue at two alphas. Fading the accent to
  a transparent *grey* instead produces a dirty halo, because the interpolation
  runs through the grey.

  ## Re-authored by the 2026-10 design pass

  The icon had to move with the palette or it would clash on the home screen:
  it was a cyan glyph in a cool blue-grey well, and the app is now warm ember on
  a cool neutral ramp. What changed is COLOUR ONLY — the geometry (108dp canvas,
  opaque edge-to-edge background, the <group> transform that places ic_mic.xml's
  path data verbatim, the radius-44 glow, the <monochrome> layer) is unchanged,
  so the safe-circle arithmetic documented in ic_launcher_foreground.xml still
  holds without recomputation.

  The background ramp is now warm-dark -> the app's own level-0 surface
  (#0A0B0F), which ties the icon to the app window rather than to a colour that
  appears nowhere in the UI.

  Measured contrast of the glyph against what is actually behind it (the glow is
  composited over the gradient, so the worst case is glyph-over-glow-over-the
  lightest end of the ramp):

      #FFA070 over #3B2117 (bare gradient start) ....... 7.43 : 1
      #FFA070 over #0A0B0F (bare gradient end) ......... 9.85 : 1
      #FFA070 over glow(0x38) over #3B2117 ............. 4.64 : 1   <- worst case
      #FFA070 over glow(0x38) over #0A0B0F ............. 6.56 : 1

  4.64:1 is the floor, against a 3:1 requirement for a glyph this size.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Warm ember-tinted dark, falling to the app's own level-0 surface. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_bg_start">#3B2117</color>
    <color name="ic_launcher_bg_end">#0A0B0F</color>

    <!-- Same hue as ic_launcher_mic at two alphas: 0x38 -> 0x00. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_glow_inner">#38FFA070</color>
    <color name="ic_launcher_glow_outer">#00FFA070</color>

    <!-- Matches dicta_accent; duplicated so a theme change cannot silently
         recolour the launcher icon without someone looking at it. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_mic">#FFA070</color>
</resources>
